## What `weapons/` (Phase H) may include

Since Phase H is the current focus, this section is explicit.

**Allowed:**
- `core/*` (Phase C) — sock, time, mem, rand, bytes, endian, log.
  All complete and tested.
- `platform/*` (Phase D) — posix/linux real syscalls. Complete and
  tested.
- Foundational `api/*` — `api/internal/types.h` (endpoint helpers,
  `xury_endpoint_is_global_v6()` etc.), `api/internal/err.h`,
  `api/internal/weapon.h` (the priority/dispatch table and weapon
  enum — this is the contract `weapons/*.c` implements against),
  `api/internal/config.h`, `api/internal/hooks.h`.
- `scan/*` (Phase F) — `scan/internal/math.h` if a weapon needs
  `xury_math_median()`, `xury_math_predict_next()`, etc. (e.g.
  `predict.c` will need this directly).
- `analysis/*` (Phase G) — classification results, if a weapon needs
  to know the classified pattern to decide how to act.
- **One specific file from Phase I when actually needed**:
  `peer/internal/mirror.h` / `peer/mirror.c`, required by `hole.c`
  only. Do not pull in `peer/relay.c` or `peer/upgrade.c` for this —
  they are not needed by any Phase H weapon.

**Not allowed:**
- Orchestration `api/*` (`api/scan.c`, `api/engine.c`, `api/peer.c`)
  — not built yet, and would be circular regardless.
- `smart/*` — `smart/learning.c` and `smart/adaptive.c` depend on
  Phase H's output (`(nat_type, weapon) -> {success, fail}`), so
  Phase H must never depend back on `smart/`. This is exactly the
  circular-dependency shape that was caught and resolved by
  splitting `learning.c` into Stage 1 (data collection, no
  dependency on weapons) and Stage 2 (decision logic, deferred until
  Phase H exists).
- `blitz/*`, `engine/*`, `sweet/*` — all higher layers, not yet
  built, would be circular.
- Any hardcoded server address, of any kind (see
  `docs/PROBING_DESIGN.md`). If a weapon needs a network target, it
  must come from a caller-supplied peer endpoint or config, never a
  literal address baked into `weapons/*.c`.

