## Rule: within a phase, order still matters

Phase D (platform) is a case that already came up: `core/sock.c`
depends on `platform/posix/sock.c` (or another platform
implementation) being present at link time, even though `core/` is
numbered before `platform/` in the phase list. In practice, write
`platform/platform.h` (the interface) before or alongside
`core/sock.c`'s dispatch logic, and confirm the platform
implementation exists before assuming a dispatch call will resolve
to something real rather than a "not implemented" error.

The same caution applies within Phase H: `weapon.c` (the dispatcher)
should be written with an interface in mind before or alongside the
first concrete weapon (`ipv6.c`), the same way `core/sock.c` and
`platform/posix/sock.c` were sequenced.

---

## What this file is not

This file does not describe *what* each module does — see
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for that. It only describes *what may include
what*, to prevent circular dependencies and stub-driven development
from recurring as new phases are built.
